.\IT2213-Full-Stack-App-Development-main\payroll-automation\README.md:151:Run `login_sample_data.sql` before `005_sample_data.sql`: the latter inserts a payment batch whose `generated_by` column references the manager account created by the login seed. `login_sample_data.sql` creates the `employee@payroll.local` account with `staff_id = NULL`, since the EMP001 staff row it should point to does not exist yet on a clean database. Once `005_sample_data.sql` inserts EMP001, it links the two with an idempotent `UPDATE user_account SET staff_id = ... WHERE email = 'employee@payroll.local'`. Final setup order is always: `005_initial_schema.sql`, then `login_sample_data.sql`, then `005_sample_data.sql`.
.\IT2213-Full-Stack-App-Development-main\payroll-automation\README.md:153:`005_sample_data.sql` creates staff EMP001-EMP008, the main 2026-07-01 to 2026-07-15 pay period plus six additional UC-005 scenario pay periods covering every state: an approved period ready for payment (with its payment batch, batch items, and payslips), a period with missing employee bank details, a batch with a failed HRMS sync, a fully completed batch with payslips, a soft-cancelled batch, a period still pending approval, and a locked period with no staff or payroll lines (an honest empty state). All payroll values (gross pay, incentive pay, CPF, SDL, net pay) and approval decisions are fixed upstream-approved values written directly to the corresponding tables; the seed file does not perform payroll calculations or approval logic itself.
.\IT2213-Full-Stack-App-Development-main\payroll-automation\README.md:155:Member 5 financial tables include `payment_batch`, immutable `payment_batch_item` snapshots, and `payslip`. Payment batch items preserve the exact approved values and secured banking data used at generation time even if upstream records later change.
.\IT2213-Full-Stack-App-Development-main\payroll-automation\README.md:169:The Phase 7 frontend is complete. It uses React Hook Form and Yup for forms, Day.js for dates, Material UI for the responsive interface, protected and role-based routes, and Axios JWT handling. Managers can review readiness, correct missing bank details, generate and manage payment batches, download secured CSV files, retry HRMS sync, cancel eligible batches, and view payslips. Employees are directed to their own payslips and cannot access manager screens.
